Perfect! Now let me compile a comprehensive summary of everything I've discovered:

## Design System Token Architecture Reference - Complete Analysis

I've thoroughly explored the imgen design system reference implementation. Here's the complete breakdown:

---

### 1. TOKEN CONTRACT (Source of Truth)

**File**: `/home/chapel/Projects/imgen/packages/design-system/src/token-contract.css`

The token contract defines 31 CSS custom properties that every design theme MUST implement:

#### Color Tokens (16):
```css
--design-bg              /* Main background */
--design-fg              /* Main foreground/text */
--design-card            /* Card/panel backgrounds */
--design-card-fg         /* Text on cards */
--design-primary         /* Active/committed: buttons, selected chips, CTAs, progress */
--design-primary-fg      /* Text on primary backgrounds */
--design-secondary       /* Secondary action color */
--design-secondary-fg    /* Text on secondary */
--design-muted           /* Disabled/deemphasized backgrounds */
--design-muted-fg        /* Disabled/deemphasized text */
--design-accent          /* Decorative + hover: eyebrows, markers, glow, shimmer, hover states */
--design-accent-fg       /* Text on accent backgrounds */
--design-destructive     /* Error/delete actions */
--design-border          /* Border color */
--design-input           /* Input field backgrounds */
--design-ring            /* Focus ring color */
```

#### Radius Tokens (4):
```css
--design-radius-sm       /* 0.25rem (4px) */
--design-radius-md       /* 0.375rem (6px) */
--design-radius-lg       /* 0.5rem (8px) */
--design-radius-xl       /* 0.75rem (12px) */
```

#### Spacing Tokens (7):
```css
--design-spacing-xs      /* 0.25rem (4px) */
--design-spacing-sm      /* 0.5rem (8px) */
--design-spacing-md      /* 1rem (16px) */
--design-spacing-lg      /* 1.5rem (24px) */
--design-spacing-xl      /* 2rem (32px) */
--design-spacing-2xl     /* 3rem (48px) */
--design-spacing-3xl     /* 4rem (64px) */
```

#### Z-Index Layers (7):
```css
--design-z-base          /* 0 (default layer) */
--design-z-dropdown      /* 10 (dropdown menus) */
--design-z-sticky        /* 20 (sticky nav, pinned elements) */
--design-z-overlay       /* 30 (backdrop overlays) */
--design-z-modal         /* 40 (dialogs, lightbox) */
--design-z-popover       /* 50 (tooltips, popovers on top of modals) */
--design-z-toast         /* 60 (toast notifications, always on top) */
```

#### Font Tokens (3, injected by next/font):
```css
--font-design-primary
--font-design-secondary
--font-design-mono
```

---

### 2. INTERACTION LANGUAGE

The design system establishes a clear semantic progression:
- **Neutral** (default state)
- **Accent** (hover/anticipation) - used on hover states
- **Primary** (active/selected/committed) - buttons, CTAs, selected chips, progress

**Example flow**: Buttons start neutral → accent on hover → primary when selected/active

---

### 3. THEME ARCHITECTURE PATTERN

Each design defines its own theme file scoped by `[data-design="N"]`:

**File structure**:
```
/packages/designs/NN/src/theme.css
```

**Pattern**: Multiple theme declarations within single file, overriding root tokens:

```css
[data-design="4"],
[data-design="4"][data-theme="dark"] {
  --design-bg: oklch(0.05 0 0);
  --design-fg: oklch(0.98 0 0);
  /* ... all 31+ tokens ... */
}

[data-design="4"][data-theme="light"] {
  --design-bg: oklch(0.96 0.015 85);
  --design-fg: oklch(0.15 0 0);
  /* ... theme-specific overrides ... */
}
```

**Key observations**:
- Uses **OKLCH color space** (not hex/rgb) for semantic, perceptually-uniform colors
- Supports **light/dark theme variants** via `data-theme` attribute
- Allows **extended design-specific tokens** (e.g., LED indicators, LCD displays, brushed metal textures)
- **Fallback tokens** defined at `:root` for pages outside `[data-design]` scope

---

### 4. TOKEN NAMING CONVENTION

**Pattern**: `--design-[semantic-name][-variant]`

Examples from actual usage:
- `--design-bg` (background)
- `--design-card-fg` (foreground text on card)
- `--design-primary-fg` (foreground on primary)
- `--design-led-green` (design-specific LED status)
- `--design-record-hover` (design-specific record button states)
- `--design-watermark-opacity` (design-specific extended property)

---

### 5. ANIMATION KEYFRAMES (Complete List)

All animations use `@keyframes` and respect `prefers-reduced-motion`:

#### Batch & Selection:
```css
@keyframes ds-batch-pulse {
  0%, 100% { transform: scale(1); }
  50% { transform: scale(1.3); }
}
```

#### Generation Bar:
```css
@keyframes ds-gen-breathe {
  0%, 100% {
    box-shadow:
      0 0 0 0 color-mix(in oklch, var(--design-accent), transparent 90%),
      inset 0 0 20px color-mix(in oklch, var(--design-accent), transparent 95%);
  }
  50% {
    box-shadow:
      0 0 20px 2px color-mix(in oklch, var(--design-accent), transparent 80%),
      inset 0 0 30px color-mix(in oklch, var(--design-accent), transparent 90%);
  }
}

@keyframes ds-gen-progress {
  from { width: 0%; }
  to { width: 100%; }
}

@keyframes ds-controls-reveal {
  from {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(-10px);
  }
  to {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
  }
}
```

#### Image Lightbox:
```css
@keyframes ds-lightbox-fade-in {
  from { opacity: 0; }
  to { opacity: 1; }
}

@keyframes ds-lightbox-scale-in {
  from {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: scale(0.95);
  }
  to {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: scale(1);
  }
}

@keyframes ds-sibling-spin {
  to { transform: rotate(360deg); }
}

@keyframes ds-failed-image-spin {
  to { transform: rotate(360deg); }
}
```

#### Skeleton/Loading:
```css
@keyframes ds-skeleton-progress-sweep {
  0% {
    transform: translateX(-100%);
    left: 0;
  }
  100% {
    transform: translateX(100%);
    left: 100%;
  }
}

@keyframes ds-skeleton-shimmer {
  0% { background-position: 200% 0; }
  100% { background-position: -200% 0; }
}
```

#### Onboarding:
```css
@keyframes ds-onboarding-bounce {
  0%, 100% { transform: translateY(0); }
  50% { transform: translateY(-4px); }
}

@keyframes ds-onboarding-point {
  0%, 100% { transform: translateX(-50%) translateY(0); }
  50% { transform: translateX(-50%) translateY(-6px); }
}
```

#### Style Switcher:
```css
@keyframes ds-style-panel-in {
  from {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(8px) scale(0.96);
  }
  to {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0) scale(1);
  }
}
```

#### Workflow Progress:
```css
@keyframes ds-workflow-shimmer {
  0% { background-position: 200% 0; }
  100% { background-position: -200% 0; }
}
```

**Common durations**: 300ms (controls), 2s (shimmer), 3s (breathing), 1.5s (progress sweep), 600ms (image zoom)

---

### 6. ORGANIZATION & NAMING PATTERNS

#### CSS Classes:
All component classes use **`.ds-` prefix** (design-system):
- `.ds-gen-bar` - generation bar container
- `.ds-skeleton-shimmer` - skeleton shimmer effect
- `.ds-lightbox-fade-in` - lightbox animation
- `.ds-gallery-card` - gallery card component

#### File Organization:
```
src/
├── token-contract.css          # Documentation only
├── index.ts                    # Main export barrel
├── COMPONENT_REGISTRY.ts       # Agent-readable component catalog
├── lib/
│   └── style-storage.ts        # Storage key helpers
├── hooks/
│   ├── use-style-switcher.ts   # Theme/style switching
│   ├── use-scroll-reveal.ts    # Scroll animations
│   └── ...
└── components/
    ├── generation-bar/
    │   ├── generation-bar.tsx
    │   └── generation-bar.css
    ├── image-lightbox/
    ├── gallery-card/
    ├── skeleton-card/
    └── ...
```

---

### 7. INTEGRATION WITH TAILWIND

The gallery app's globals.css maps design tokens to Tailwind theme:

```css
